## PART TEN — AUDITS AND COMPLIANCE

Regulators will ask: “Prove that your rules were enforced.” UICP enables this.

### Proving rules were enforced

Give the auditor the exported audit bundle (`audit_export/`). They can:

1. Verify the `manifest.json` integrity hash.
2. Walk the cryptographic chain to confirm no decision was added or removed.
3. Verify Ed25519 signatures using the public keys in `public_keys.json`.
4. See exactly which constraint was violated for every BLOCK decision.

No access to UICP, the AI model, or any internal engine is required.

### Proving rules are correct

Keep a record of:

* Who wrote each rule.
* Why the rule exists (which regulation or policy).
* Who approved it.
* When it was deployed.

### Proving no one bypasses UICP

Your application architecture must route every AI decision through the `/enforce` endpoint before the decision takes effect. Document this in your system architecture diagram and make it available to auditors.

